# Dialogue: introduction scene
dlg-prologue_01 = The kingdom of Valenwood is dying beneath a sky of ink and ash. A storm of black lightning tears the heavens without respite.
dlg-prologue_02 = This is the work of Lord Muldant. Entrenched in Nareff castle, he guards the Ancestral Stone, which holds the gates of the abyss wide open.
dlg-prologue_03 = Night and day, packs of nightmarish creatures pour out, devouring the world's life force and keeping all life from flourishing.
dlg-prologue_04 = I am Samélia, princess of the elves, and I refuse to watch my people fade away. You are the four greatest heroes of the free lands.
dlg-prologue_05 = Your mission: infiltrate the dungeon of Nareff, slay the dark lord and break the power of the stone.
dlg-prologue_06 = My armor is blessed, princess. My sword and my body will shield the company.
dlg-prologue_07 = The ancient curses of that fortress will soon hold no secrets from me.
dlg-prologue_08 = My bow will bring down the sentries before they can raise the alarm.
dlg-prologue_09 = And my hammer will break down their iron doors!
dlg-intro_e0 = This is the forest of Valenwood. Courage, every step brings you closer to Nareff!
dlg-intro_01 = The forest is silent. Too silent. Stay together.
dlg-intro_02 = Silent? Listen... far away, the castle is whispering. Can't you hear it?
dlg-intro_03 = All I hear is wind and trouble. Keep your eyes open.
dlg-intro_04 = Trouble? Perfect! I brought enough to blow everything up!
dlg-intro_05 = Not at my back. And not without my order.
dlg-intro_06 = A few pointers. To move: %move%. To strike: %attack%.
dlg-intro_07 = For the special power of the hero you control: %special%.
dlg-intro_08 = %action% to act on what's around us, and %switch% to switch to the next hero.
dlg-bridge_e1 = The marsh is more dangerous than the forest. That broken bridge is the monsters' doing: without it, Nareff stays out of reach.
dlg-intro_e5 = Go now, and may the light guide you! My heart is with you.
dlg-bridge_01 = The marsh bridge is broken. Without it, we can't reach the far bank.
dlg-bridge_02 = Some wood, some iron, a little patience: I can put it right again.
dlg-bridge_03 = I just need a spare part, hidden somewhere in the clearings.
dlg-bridge_04 = Wolves prowl, and the marsh hides worse. Keep your eyes open.
dlg-bridge_05 = When you find it, switch to the Forgebraise with %switch% (as many times as needed), then head to the bridge.
dlg-bridge_panel_01 = There's the job: a jammed mechanism, just as expected.
dlg-bridge_panel_02 = With the spare part, I'll handle it. Take my place (%switch%) and hold %action% in front of it.
dlg-bridge_panel_03 = We've got you covered. Hurry before the wolves come back.
dlg-drawbridge_01 = The castle, at last. But the drawbridge is raised.
dlg-drawbridge_02 = Its chain runs past a target, over there. One well-placed arrow and it comes down.
dlg-drawbridge_03 = I'm missing the target's disc. It must be lying around in the clearings.
dlg-drawbridge_04 = What if I melted the chain?
dlg-drawbridge_05 = If you want to find it at the bottom of the moat... Switch heroes with %switch% to hand me control.
dlg-drawbridge_06 = They say guards are locked in cages along the road. Let's free them if we can.
dlg-drawbridge_panel_01 = The target's mount: its disc is missing.
dlg-drawbridge_panel_02 = I fix it by holding %action% in front of it, then shoot it: one shot (%attack%) is enough.
dlg-gate_01 = The castle's great gate. And the pack has no intention of letting us near.
dlg-gate_02 = The gate is sealed by a rune. I can dispel it, but I need three violet crystals.
dlg-gate_03 = The beasts surely keep some. They are their favorite toys.
dlg-gate_04 = Then we knock them out, pick them up, and come back.
dlg-gate_05 = Switch to the Sorcerer (%switch%) when the time comes. For now, let's deal with the pack.
dlg-gate_panel_01 = The seal. Three empty sockets, as I thought.
dlg-gate_panel_02 = With the three crystals I'll dispel it: take my place (%switch%) and hold %action% in front of the rune.
dlg-knight_01 = The crypts. At the far end, the royal door: a mass of steel nobody has passed in centuries.
dlg-knight_02 = No spell will make it yield. This isn't a matter of magic.
dlg-knight_03 = Nor bombs, so they say. What a shame.
dlg-knight_04 = Then it's up to you, Knight. Take the lead: %switch% switches heroes.
dlg-knight_05 = My blade and my shield. When the dead rise, my Bulwark (%special%) protects the whole team.
dlg-knight_door_01 = There's the royal door. It will take strength and courage.
dlg-knight_door_02 = Take my place (%switch%) and hold %action% against the door. Stay behind me: the Bulwark (%special%) will cover you.
dlg-castle_01 = Another royal door. Same fight, but this time we all know how to use our talents.
dlg-castle_02 = Guarded by three obstacles, one for each of us.
dlg-castle_03 = A violet ward, a jammed mechanism, a portcullis... Work for everyone!
dlg-castle_04 = And we'll need to find what beats them: crystals, a spare part, a target disc.
dlg-castle_05 = When all is done, the door itself is mine. Gather what we need.
dlg-castle_06 = I can see a cage in the distance, with a green figure inside... It's Princess Samélia!
dlg-castle_07 = Let's free her: she has stood by us too long to leave her behind.

# Dialogue: the royal door
dlg-royal_door_01 = The royal door. I can't get near it: an enchantment pushes me back.
dlg-royal_door_02 = A violet ward. I can dispel it, but I need three ingredients. They must be lying around the castle.
dlg-royal_door_03 = And that orange mechanism is completely jammed! I need a spare part.
dlg-royal_door_04 = That portcullis is mine: an arrow has to hit a target. We still have to find the target disc.
dlg-royal_door_05 = Good. Everyone has a colour: violet for the Sorcerer, orange for the Forgebraise, green for the Ranger.
dlg-royal_door_06 = As for the door itself, it is steel. It will take strength and courage. That one is mine.
dlg-puzzle_rune_01 = A circle of violet runes. Three empty sockets: I need three ingredients.
dlg-puzzle_rune_02 = Violet crystals, most likely. Let's find them, and I'll dispel the ward right here.
dlg-puzzle_rune_03 = Bring back three. We'll cover you.
dlg-puzzle_gears_01 = A jammed mechanism! A bent bar is wedged in the orange gears.
dlg-puzzle_gears_02 = With the spare part, orange as well, I can get it running again. It's lying around somewhere.
dlg-puzzle_gears_03 = I'll point it out if I see it. Don't take it out on the rust.
dlg-puzzle_target_01 = An empty bracket, all green. The target disc is missing.
dlg-puzzle_target_02 = Once the disc is fixed, an arrow has to hit it: that's what raises the portcullis.
dlg-puzzle_target_03 = An arrow, mind you. Not a spell. Be precise.

# Dialogue: the locked alcove
dlg-alcove_01 = A locked alcove. I could blow it open.
dlg-alcove_opt_key = Let's look for a key.
dlg-alcove_opt_boom = Boom!
dlg-alcove_02 = Wise. Monsters and generators sometimes carry one.
dlg-alcove_03 = Uh... my bombs aren't ready yet. Let's find a key.

